text: "---\nmodule: \"02-CLIENT-ACQUISITION\"\npart: \"B\"\ntitle: \"Cold Outreach Playbook\"\nversion: \"2026.05\"\nstatus: \"Production-Ready\"\n---\n\n# 02B: Cold Outreach Playbook\n\n> **Core Principle:** A great template is a starting point, but true success comes from combining proven structure with deep personalization and executing efficiently.\n>\n> *\"The difference between 3% reply rates and 15% reply rates is not creativity. It is process.\"* [^34^]\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [The Anatomy of a High-Converting Cold Email](#1-the-anatomy-of-a-high-converting-cold-email)\n2. [Freelance-Specific Templates](#2-freelance-specific-templates)\n3. [Follow-Up Sequences](#3-follow-up-sequences)\n4. [DM & LinkedIn Outreach](#4-dm--linkedin-outreach)\n5. [Deliverability & Infrastructure](#5-deliverability--infrastructure)\n6. [AI Prompts](#6-ai-prompts)\n7. [Action Checklist](#7-action-checklist)\n\n---\n\n## 1. The Anatomy of a High-Converting Cold Email\n\n### The 4-Part Structure [^28^][^34^]\n\n```\n[SIGNAL-LED OPENER] → [PAIN POINT BRIDGE] → [SOCIAL PROOF] → [LOW-COMMITMENT CTA]\n```\n\n| Part | Purpose | Length | Example |\n|------|---------|--------|---------|\n| **Opener** | Show you did research | 1-2 sentences | \"Noticed [Company] just launched [Product] — congrats on the release.\" |\n| **Bridge** | Connect their situation to your solution | 1 sentence | \"Most teams I work with see [pain point] after launching [similar product].\" |\n| **Proof** | Demonstrate you've solved this before | 1-2 sentences | \"We helped [Similar Company] reduce [metric] by [result] in [timeframe].\" |\n| **CTA** | Make it easy to say yes | 1 question | \"Worth a 15-min call this week to explore?\" |\n\n### Subject Line Rules\n\n| Rule | Do | Don't |\n|------|-----|-------|\n| Length | 3-7 words | Long, vague subjects |\n| Curiosity | Create a gap | Give everything away |\n| Personalization | Include company name | Generic \"Quick question\" |\n| Urgency | Soft, not pushy | \"URGENT\" or \"RE:\" tricks |\n| Relevance | Reference recent event | Random cold pitch |\n\n### Subject Line Templates\n\n| Template | Example |\n|----------|---------|\n| `[Company] + [Outcome]` | \"AcmeCorp + AI Pipeline\" |\n| `Question about [Recent Event]` | \"Question about your Series A\" |\n| `[Mutual Connection] suggested I reach out` | \"Sarah Chen suggested I reach out\" |\n| `Quick idea for [Company]'s [Department]` | \"Quick idea for Acme's data team\" |\n| `[Result] for [Similar Company]` | \"40% churn reduction for SaaS teams\" |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Freelance-Specific Templates\n\n### Template 1: The Ultra-Short Value Offer [^31^]\n\n**Best for:** Any freelancer with a portfolio\n**Benchmark:** 8-10% reply rate when offer is genuinely useful\n**Length:** 40-60 words\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nNoticed {{company}} just {{context trigger}}. I put together a quick \nLoom auditing your {{specific thing}} with 3 fixes.\n\nWorth a look?\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n**Example for AI/ML Freelancer:**\n```\nHi Sarah,\n\nNoticed DataFlow just launched your real-time analytics dashboard. \nI recorded a 3-min Loom reviewing your ML pipeline architecture \nwith 2 scalability risks and 1 quick win.\n\nWorth a look?\n\nAlex\n```\n\n**Why it works:**\n- Proves competence before asking for anything\n- Low friction (just watch a video)\n- Specific to their situation (not generic)\n- Creates reciprocity (you gave value first)\n\n### Template 2: The Portfolio Proof [^31^]\n\n**Best for:** Freelancers with strong case studies\n**Benchmark:** 5-8% reply rate\n**Length:** 50-70 words\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nI helped {{similar_company}} increase {{metric}} by {{result}} — \nhere's the case study: {{link}}.\n\nI spotted a few places {{company}} could see similar gains. \nOpen to a quick chat this week?\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\nHi Marcus,\n\nI helped FinTechFlow reduce model deployment time from 3 weeks to \n3 days — here's how: [link].\n\nI noticed CloudScale's current ML setup has similar bottlenecks. \nOpen to a 15-min call to explore?\n\nAlex\n```\n\n### Template 3: The \"Right Person?\" Ask [^31^]\n\n**Best for:** When you don't know who owns the budget\n**Benchmark:** High forward rate (gets passed to right person)\n**Length:** 30-50 words\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nI help {{type of company}} with {{specific outcome}}. Who'd be the \nbest person to talk to about {{specific thing}} at {{company}}?\n\nThanks,\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\nHi Jordan,\n\nI help B2B SaaS teams productionize ML models in 4-6 weeks. \nWho'd be the best person to talk to about your AI roadmap at \nDataSync?\n\nThanks,\nAlex\n```\n\n### Template 4: The Problem-Agitation-Solution (PAS)\n\n**Best for:** Technical audiences who understand the pain\n**Benchmark:** 6-9% reply rate\n**Length:** 80-120 words\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nMost {{type of company}} I speak with have a frustrating pattern:\n\nThey build great ML models in Jupyter notebooks...\nBut 6 months later, those models are still not in production.\n\nThe result? $40K+/year in data science salary with $0 in business value.\n\nI help teams close that gap in 3-4 weeks with production MLOps pipelines.\n\nWorth a 15-min call to see if there's a fit?\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n### Template 5: The Referral / Mutual Intro [^33^]\n\n**Best for:** Warm introductions\n**Benchmark:** 15-25% reply rate (warm leads)\n**Length:** 50-70 words\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\n{{Referrer's name}} suggested I reach out. They mentioned you're \nfocused on {{priority}} and wrestling with {{brief pain}}.\n\nWe've supported {{referrer or peer}} with {{one-line result}}.\n\nIf helpful, I can share a short overview and tailor a demo to \n{{recipient's team or KPI}}. Would {{two time options}} work?\n\nThanks,\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Follow-Up Sequences\n\n### The 5-Email Sequence [^30^]\n\n| Email | Day | Purpose | Length | Tone |\n|-------|-----|---------|--------|------|\n| **Initial** | 1 | First contact + value offer | 50-70 words | Helpful |\n| **Bump** | 3 | Gentle reminder | <50 words | Casual |\n| **New Value** | 7 | Share resource/insight | 80-100 words | Educational |\n| **Social Proof** | 10 | Case study or result | 60-80 words | Confident |\n| **Breakup** | 14 | Acknowledge silence, offer out | <40 words | Respectful |\n\n### Email 2: The Gentle Bump (Day 3)\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nQuick bump — my Loom on {{topic}} is still sitting in your inbox.\n\nNo rush, just didn't want it to get buried.\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n### Email 3: New Value (Day 7)\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nSaw this {{article/report/statistic}} on {{topic}} and thought of you:\n\n{{One-line summary + link}}\n\nThe part about {{specific insight}} aligns with what we discussed \naround {{their pain point}}.\n\nNo pitch — just thought you'd find it useful.\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n### Email 4: Social Proof (Day 10)\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nWanted to share a quick win from a {{similar company}}:\n\n{{One-line result with metric}}\n\nThe interesting part? They had the exact same setup as {{company}} \n{{specific similarity}}.\n\nHappy to share the full case study if helpful.\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n### Email 5: The Breakup (Day 14)\n\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nTotally understand if timing isn't right — budgets, priorities, \nroadmaps shift.\n\nI'll pause my follow-ups here. If {{topic}} becomes relevant later, \nmy door's open.\n\nWishing you and {{company}} a great {{quarter/year}}.\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n### The Follow-Up Rules [^28^]\n\n| Rule | Specification |\n|------|--------------|\n| **Frequency** | Every 2-3 days, not daily |\n| **Total attempts** | 5-8 touches over 2-4 weeks |\n| **Value escalation** | Each follow-up adds new value |\n| **Tone shift** | Helpful → Casual → Educational → Confident → Respectful |\n| **Opt-out** | Always offer an easy \"no\" |\n| **Tracking** | Log every touch in spreadsheet/CRM |\n\n---\n\n## 4. DM & LinkedIn Outreach\n\n### LinkedIn DM Templates\n\n**Template 1: Post Engagement → DM**\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nReally enjoyed your post on {{topic}} — especially your point about \n{{specific insight}}.\n\nI help {{target}} with {{outcome}} and see this challenge daily. \nWould love to connect and learn more about your work at {{company}}.\n\nBest,\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n**Template 2: Connection Request + Immediate DM**\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nThanks for connecting! \n\nI noticed {{company}} is {{recent activity/signal}}. I specialize in \n{{specific outcome}} for teams like yours.\n\nWorth a quick chat to explore if there's a fit?\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n**Template 3: The \"Loom DM\"**\n```\nHi {{first_name}},\n\nI recorded a 2-min video specifically for {{company}} reviewing your \n{{website/product/feature}} with 2 quick wins.\n\n{{Loom link}}\n\nNo pitch — just thought you'd find it useful.\n\n{{Your name}}\n```\n\n### The LinkedIn 15-15-15 Ritual\n\n| Time | Activity | Count | Purpose |\n|------|----------|-------|---------|\n| Morning (30 min) | Send DMs to new prospects | 15 | Initiate conversations |\n| Noon (30 min) | Comment on target posts | 15 | Build visibility + rapport |\n| Evening (30 min) | Send connection requests | 15 | Expand network |\n\n### DM Tracking Spreadsheet\n\n| Column | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| Name | Prospect name |\n| Company | Company name |\n| Title | Job title |\n| Source | Where you found them |\n| Signal | What triggered outreach |\n| Date Sent | When you first contacted |\n| Template Used | Which template |\n| Response | Yes/No/Pending |\n| Follow-Up 1 | Date + status |\n| Follow-Up 2 | Date + status |\n| Follow-Up 3 | Date + status |\n| Notes | Any context |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Deliverability & Infrastructure\n\n### The 10-Day Domain Warm-Up [^31^]\n\n| Day | Activity | Volume |\n|-----|----------|--------|\n| 1 | Set up SPF, DKIM, DMARC | 0 |\n| 2-3 | Send 5 personal emails/day | 5/day |\n| 4 | First 5 cold emails | 5 |\n| 7 | Follow-up #1 + 5 new emails | 10 |\n| 10 | Follow-up #2 + 5 new emails | 10 |\n\n### Email Authentication Setup\n\n| Record | Purpose | How to Set Up |\n|--------|---------|---------------|\n| **SPF** | Authorizes sending servers | DNS TXT record |\n| **DKIM** | Cryptographic signature | Email provider settings |\n| **DMARC** | Policy + reporting | DNS TXT record |\n\n### Tools for Deliverability\n\n| Tool | Purpose | Cost |\n|------|---------|------|\n| **Mail-Tester.com** | Spam score check | Free |\n| **GlockApps** | Inbox placement testing | Freemium |\n| **Warmup Inbox** | Automated domain warming | $9/mo |\n| **Saleshandy** | Built-in warm-up | Included in plan |\n\n### Reply Rate Benchmarks (2026)\n\n| Outreach Type | Good | Great | Elite |\n|---------------|------|-------|-------|\n| Cold email (generic) | 1-2% | 3-5% | — |\n| Cold email (personalized) | 5-8% | 10-15% | 20%+ |\n| LinkedIn DM (warm) | 10-15% | 20-30% | 40%+ |\n| LinkedIn DM (cold) | 5-10% | 15-20% | — |\n| Referral intro | 20-30% | 40-50% | 60%+ |\n\n---\n\n## 6. AI Prompts\n\n### Prompt 1: Cold Email Personalizer\n\n```\nAct as a cold email specialist for B2B technical services.\n\nProspect details:\n- Name: {{name}}\n- Company: {{company}}\n- Title: {{title}}\n- Recent signal: {{signal}}\n- Company size: {{size}}\n- Industry: {{industry}}\n\nMy service: {{your service}}\nMy differentiator: {{what makes you unique}}\nRecent win: {{case study result}}\n\nWrite 3 cold email variations:\n1. Ultra-short value offer (40-60 words)\n2. Portfolio proof approach (50-70 words)\n3. Problem-agitation-solution (80-100 words)\n\nFor each:\n- Subject line (3-7 words)\n- Body text\n- CTA\n- Estimated reply rate based on 2026 benchmarks\n\nRules:\n- Reference their specific signal\n- Include one number (metric or result)\n- No generic \"I hope you're well\"\n- Offer value before asking for call\n```\n\n### Prompt 2: Follow-Up Sequence Generator\n\n```\nAct as a follow-up sequence architect.\n\nContext:\n- Initial email sent: {{date}}\n- Template used: {{template type}}\n- Prospect: {{title}} at {{company}}\n- Signal: {{their situation}}\n\nCreate a 5-email follow-up sequence:\n\nEmail 1 (Day 3): Gentle bump\n- Reference initial email briefly\n- Add new value angle\n- Under 50 words\n\nEmail 2 (Day 7): New value\n- Don't mention previous emails\n- Share relevant resource/insight\n- Different angle on same problem\n- Include link to content\n\nEmail 3 (Day 10): Social proof\n- Brief case study or result\n- Similar company/role\n- Specific number/metric\n\nEmail 4 (Day 14): Breakup\n- Acknowledge silence\n- Offer easy out\n- Leave door open\n- Under 40 words\n\nFor each email:\n- Subject line\n- Body text\n- Word count\n- Timing notes\n- Expected psychology (why it works)\n```\n\n### Prompt 3: Objection Response Generator\n\n```\nAct as a sales objection handler for freelance services.\n\nCreate responses to these common objections:\n\n1. \"Not interested\"\n2. \"Bad timing / Too busy\"\n3. \"Already using [competitor]\"\n4. \"Send me more information\"\n5. \"Need to talk to my team/boss\"\n6. \"Your rate is too high\"\n7. \"We've tried this before and it didn't work\"\n8. \"We're building this in-house\"\n\nFor each response:\n- Under 50 words\n- Maintains relationship\n- Moves conversation forward\n- Sounds natural, not scripted\n- Includes one question to re-engage\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Action Checklist\n\n### Day 1-3: Infrastructure\n\n- [ ] Set up professional email domain (not Gmail)\n- [ ] Configure SPF, DKIM, DMARC records\n- [ ] Set up Apollo.io or Hunter.io account\n- [ ] Create outreach tracking spreadsheet\n- [ ] Write 5 template variations\n- [ ] Test templates with Mail-Tester.com\n\n### Day 4-7: First Sends\n\n- [ ] Send 5 cold emails/day (personalized)\n- [ ] Send 10 LinkedIn DMs/day\n- [ ] Track all activity in spreadsheet\n- [ ] Note response rate by template\n- [ ] A/B test subject lines\n\n### Day 8-14: Follow-Up Engine\n\n- [ ] Send follow-up #1 to non-responders\n- [ ] Send 5 new cold emails/day\n- [ ] Send follow-up #2 to non-responders\n- [ ] Analyze which templates perform best\n- [ ] Refine based on data\n\n### Day 15-30: Optimization\n\n- [ ] Calculate true reply rate by channel\n- [ ] Double down on highest-performing template\n- [ ] Build \"dream 100\" list for personalized outreach\n- [ ] Set up automated sequences (Reply.io or similar)\n- [ ] Review and iterate monthly\n\n---\n\n> **Next:** [02C: Platform Strategy →](02C-PLATFORM-STRATEGY.md)\n>\n> *\"The fortune is in the follow-up. But the follow-up only works if the first email is right.\"*\n\n---\n\n*Module 02B | Cold Outreach Playbook | Version 2026.05*\n"
